Subject: [PATCH] usb: chipidea: msm: enable the short-packet SG workaround

On Samsung A5 (MSM8916), a FunctionFS AIO download of 41054 bytes fails
with "not page aligned sg buffer" and -EINVAL. The final short SG entry
can require DMA bouncing, losing the page alignment required by the
ChipIdea dTD builder. The existing SG repair path is gated by
CI_HDRC_HAS_SHORT_PKT_LIMIT, which the MSM glue does not set.

Enable that existing workaround for the MSM controller: problem SG tails
are replaced with a page-sized buffer before DMA mapping. This also
selects the existing 16 KiB request handling limit for this controller.

This is a local hardware bring-up patch; wider MSM coverage remains to
be tested. See the A5 experiment log for reproduction and validation.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c b/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c
--- a/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/chipidea/ci_hdrc_msm.c
@@ -189,7 +189,8 @@ static int ci_hdrc_msm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ci->pdata.capoffset = DEF_CAPOFFSET;
 	ci->pdata.flags	= CI_HDRC_REGS_SHARED | CI_HDRC_DISABLE_STREAMING |
 			  CI_HDRC_OVERRIDE_AHB_BURST |
-			  CI_HDRC_OVERRIDE_PHY_CONTROL;
+			  CI_HDRC_OVERRIDE_PHY_CONTROL |
+			  CI_HDRC_HAS_SHORT_PKT_LIMIT;
 	ci->pdata.notify_event = ci_hdrc_msm_notify_event;
 
 	reset = devm_reset_control_get(&pdev->dev, "core");
